ng for me we had mr. robot tell  Magda  and young Elliot in the boardroom that  Darlene might be the key so we just had  that introduced recently DOM is not the  important one here Darlene is definitely  the key character after you had to pick  one of the two so Dom being left behind  to deal with the tragedy of Darlene  being killed on a flight that they were  on together that doesn't really work  like where do they fit that into the  last three hours so as I was watching it  I was just sort of like well this  doesn't really feel right it doesn't  feel right and then it turned into this  thing where Tom starts to leave  Darlene starts to freak out she starts  to have a panic attack they got this pop  song in the background Tom gets to the  exit can't go through it  Darlene gets to the ticket gate can't  scan or ticket goes into the bathroom  and goes into full-blown panic attack  Tom boards the plane just missing  Darlene as she ran into the bathroom  Darlene works her way through the panic  attack in it this is a pretty good  moment here where the woman's asking her  behind her if she needs help and she  says no I can take care of myself and  that really is the big moment where she  comes to that understanding and I also  really like the fact that when dawn lets  go she decides not to get up she just  sits back she's able to sleep on the  plane  everyone was telling her that she needed  to get some sleep and she finally does  in the end it all works out I feel like  this could be the last time we see Dom I  feel like it will work as an ending for  her character as far as what's going on  in the rest of the story Darlene I think  has a part to play so I definitely don't  think that's the last we're gonna see of  her but it could be and with three  episodes left that's where we're at we  did find out that the finale will be a  two-parter it's gonna air on the same  night so we have two more installments  with mr. robot to come it feels like the  dark Army has been s